    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Enforcement agents intercepted a surge in unauthorized crossings along the southwest border, with apprehensions climbing from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March as seasonal conditions facilitated movement. Security analysts note that despite this statistical trend, strict policies have successfully contained the border crisis, keeping year-to-date crossings near multi-decade lows. The federal enforcement agency continues its mission at the U.S. border, though political dysfunction hampers institutional capacity to secure the border as legislators remain deadlocked over separate funding for immigration enforcement agencies.",
