    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The federal enforcement agency operating at the U.S. border recorded a notable increase in apprehensions along the southwest border, rising from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March. Data monitors tracking border security metrics attribute this numerical change partly to milder spring weather encouraging border crossers. Despite the enforcement policy outcome maintaining low crossing numbers under asylum shutdown and deportation policies, lawmakers remain deadlocked over funding for immigration enforcement agencies, creating a legislative stalemate that hinders further institutional response.",
