    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "Political dysfunction continues to hamper institutional capacity to secure the border as elected officials remain deadlocked over separate funding for immigration enforcement agencies in a pending reconciliation package. This government impasse persists even as spring weather conditions have facilitated movement, contributing to an increase in apprehensions along the southwest border from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March. While enforcement agents intercept individuals attempting unauthorized entry, the border security effect of existing policies maintains immigration statistics near multi-decade lows, yet the funding dispute prevents decisive action from political leadership.",
